argument:
I’m not convinced our team should play so defensively at home. We’ve got fast wings; it seems like a waste to sit back all game.

@northstand Maybe, but we’ve also conceded early when we pushed too hard. A cautious start could keep us in it.

Good point. If they press late, the wings can still stretch the field once the other side tires.

My manager says the team should move to shorter meetings, and honestly I agree.
@Leena Same, but only if we send agendas ahead of time. Otherwise short meetings just become rushed meetings.
@Gus That’s the part people forget. A tighter schedule helps, but the prep work matters just as much.

The update made the game look nicer on my laptop, but the frame drops are rough in crowded areas.
@Sera I noticed that too. It runs fine in smaller maps, so maybe the patch hit certain effects harder than others.
Could be. If they fix the performance without changing the visuals again, I’d be happy.
